# When API_KEYS is set, add "Authorization: Bearer {{apiKey}}" to /events and /alerts requests.
@apiKey = change-me

### 1. Ingest a failed login event
POST http://localhost:8080/events
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "timestamp": "2026-04-24T10:00:00Z",
  "ip": "192.168.1.10",
  "event_type": "failed_login",
  "message": "Login attempt with wrong password"
}

###

### 2. Trigger a brute-force alert (send 5x rapidly from same IP)
POST http://localhost:8080/events
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "ip": "10.0.0.99",
  "event_type": "failed_login"
}

###

### 3. SQL injection attempt
POST http://localhost:8080/events
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "ip": "203.0.113.42",
  "event_type": "http_request",
  "path": "/search?q=' OR 1=1 --",
  "user_agent": "curl/7.88"
}

###

### 4. Sensitive path access
POST http://localhost:8080/events
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "ip": "198.51.100.5",
  "event_type": "http_request",
  "path": "/.env",
  "message": "GET /.env HTTP/1.1"
}

###

### 5. Newest events (default limit 100, max 1000), optionally filtered by IP
GET http://localhost:8080/events?limit=20&ip=10.0.0.99

###

### 6. Newest alerts
GET http://localhost:8080/alerts?limit=20

###

### 7. Health check
GET http://localhost:8080/health

###

### 8. Prometheus metrics
GET http://localhost:8080/metrics

###

### 9. Batch ingestion (JSON array; NDJSON works as well)
POST http://localhost:8080/events/batch
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{apiKey}}

[
  {"ip": "198.51.100.7", "event_type": "http_request", "path": "/download?file=..%2f..%2fetc%2fpasswd", "user_agent": "sqlmap/1.7"},
  {"ip": "198.51.100.7", "event_type": "port_scan", "port": 22},
  {"ip": "not-an-ip"}
]

###

### 10. Network event (e.g. from your own sensor); 10 distinct ports from one IP trigger PortScan
POST http://localhost:8080/events
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{apiKey}}

{
  "ip": "203.0.113.5",
  "event_type": "firewall_block",
  "dst_ip": "192.0.2.10",
  "port": 22,
  "src_port": 54321,
  "protocol": "tcp",
  "direction": "inbound"
}

###

### 11. DNS query (e.g. from your own resolver); 50 distinct subdomains of one domain within a minute trigger DNSTunneling
POST http://localhost:8080/events
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{apiKey}}

{
  "ip": "192.168.1.23",
  "event_type": "dns_query",
  "domain": "c01.ZXhmaWx0cmF0ZWQ.x.evil-example.net",
  "metadata": {"base_domain": "evil-example.net", "query_type": "TXT"}
}
